To remotely push this update to everyone who already installed your app, you will use the **Auto-Updater** we built! 

Tauri's auto-updater works by checking the `updater.json` file hosted on your GitHub `main` branch. When the version in that file is higher than the version running on their computer, it automatically downloads the new `.exe`!

Here is the exact **4-step process** you need to do whenever you want to push an update (like these avatar fixes) to your users:

### Step 1: Bump the Version
Because your users already have `1.0.0` installed, they won't download an update unless the number goes up.
1. Open `package.json` and change the version to `"1.0.1"`.
2. Open [src-tauri/tauri.conf.json](cci:7://file:///d:/auravtchub/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json:0:0-0:0) and change the version to `"1.0.1"`.

### Step 2: Build & Sign 
1. Run `npm run tauri build` to generate your new `Aura VTC Hub_1.0.1_x64-setup.exe`.
2. Run your signing command to generate the new signature (`.sig`) for this specific build:
   ```powershell
   $env:TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD="1234"; npx tauri signer sign -k (Get-Content .\updater.key -Raw) "./src-tauri/target/release/bundle/nsis/Aura VTC Hub_1.0.2_x64-setup.exe"

   ```

### Step 3: Update `updater.json`
Open your `updater.json` file and manually update the 3 important fields so the app knows where to look:
- `"version": "1.0.1"`
- `"signature": "PASTE_YOUR_NEW_BASE64_SIGNATURE_HERE"`
- `"url": "https://github.com/Chetan302003/Meth-Hub/releases/download/v1.0.1/Aura.VTC.Hub_1.0.1_x64-setup.exe"`
*(Optional: Update the `"notes"` field so users know what the update fixes!)*

### Step 4: Push to GitHub
1. Commit and `git push` your code to GitHub (this pushes your modified `updater.json` so all the installed apps can instantly see it).
2. Go to your GitHub repository and **Draft a New Release**.
3. Set the Tag strictly to **`v1.0.1`**.
4. Rename your newly built `.exe` from `Aura VTC Hub_1.0.1...` to exactly **`Aura.VTC.Hub_1.0.1_x64-setup.exe`** (so it perfectly matches the URL).
5. Drag and drop the `.exe` into the release box and click **Publish**!

The next time any of your drivers open the Hub, a beautiful native Windows dialogue box will pop up saying *"Aura VTC Hub v1.0.1 is available!"* with your release notes. When they click "Update", it will smoothly download the `.exe`, verify your secure signature, and seamlessly restart the app with the newly injected avatar fixes!

